# stellar-agent-guard-sdk — live-suite environment template.
#
# Copy this to `.env.phase2` (gitignored) and fill in the values:
#
#   cp .env.phase2.example .env.phase2
#
# The suite lives in tests/integration/ and is run with `npm run test:integration`.
# It is the only thing that needs this file; the unit suite and CI never read it.
#
# Every key below is REQUIRED. tests/integration/harness.ts validates the set up
# front and fails with one message naming all missing keys at once, so an
# incomplete file only costs you one run to diagnose.
#
# Never commit the filled-in file: it holds testnet secret keys. This template
# is safe to commit because it contains key names and comments, no values.
#
# Testnet only. Never reuse these keys on any other network.
#
# ── Public identifiers (safe to share) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Address of the deployed guard smart account the suite enforces against.
PHASE2_GUARD=
# Address of the SAC test token whose transfers the suite attempts.
PHASE2_TOKEN=
# Soroban RPC endpoint. Optional — defaults to the public testnet RPC.
# Only list it in GitBook/YAML docs, not in committed code.
PHASE2_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org

# ── Secret keys (the reason this file is gitignored) ─────────────────────────
# Admin of the guard. Installs the test policy (which also clears the rolling
# window), so every window-sensitive scenario 3 case starts from a clean slate.
PHASE2_ADMIN_SECRET=
# The guard's registered agent key. Signs the guard's auth entry, so it is
# exercised by every transfer scenario: 1 (within caps), 2 (per-tx cap),
# 3 (rolling window), 5 (paused). Needs XLM to pay source fees.
PHASE2_AGENT_SECRET=
# Issuer of the SAC test token. Mints the guard's starting balance and is the
# source for reading live balances during preconditions. Not read by the suite
# itself, but required to (re)deploy with `npm run deploy:phase2`.
PHASE2_ISSUER_SECRET=
# Allowlisted transfer destination, and the only recipient scenario 1 will
# accept. Must hold a trustline to PHASE2_TOKEN or the transfer fails at the
# token contract instead of at the guard.
PHASE2_RECIPIENT_SECRET=
# Deliberately unlisted account. Exists so scenario 4 (recipient allowlist) has
# a real address to be refused; it needs no funding and no trustline.
PHASE2_OUTSIDER_SECRET=
